- **In Progress:** Committing the `file://` local-preview fix (JOURNAL.md 2026-08-19 Cline). Browsers block the WebGL 360° viewer over `file://` (unique opaque origin + no CORS → Pannellum `texImage2D` rejects the pano), so double-click open of the unzipped package can't render. Walk-through + tour-map widgets now detect `file://` and show a clear notice (`python3 -m http.server 8000` → `http://localhost:8000/…`); docs require a local server. **Loose end:** rebuild `cma-museum-walk-through.zip` so it carries the fixed HTML.
- **Newly Unblocked:** All three standalone widgets have 0 HTML `style=` attributes. Local panos are byte-identical to CMA `-scaled` CDN URLs. `file://` preview failure diagnosed and addressed in widget + docs.
- **Still Blocked:** Jane's Innovation Station + Step Up To Science are 2560×1440 (16:9) on both local and CDN — needs original 2:1 re-export + WP re-upload. Hotspot yaw/pitch still needs a human pass on each of the 12 scenes.

## WPBakery / standalone tour widgets

Self-contained HTML in `public/` (force-added — `public/*` is gitignored). Same pattern for both:

| Widget                                | Standalone URL                                                     | Embed on `#/exhibits`              |
| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------- |
| Tour the Museum (floor map + pins)    | https://mattybotstew.github.io/Homepagev2/museum-tour-map.html     | `museum-tour-map.html?embed=1`     |
| Walk-Through Tour (room-to-room 360°) | https://mattybotstew.github.io/Homepagev2/museum-walk-through.html | `museum-walk-through.html?embed=1` |

Handoff: open the standalone page → copy START→END markers into WPBakery Raw HTML. `ASSET_MODE = "auto"` (default) uses same-origin `/wp-content/uploads/…` on any WordPress / WP Engine / wpdev host; uses bundled `museum-tour-map/` files only on GitHub Pages and localhost (CMA CDN has no CORS for cross-origin). Floor-plan `<img>` defaults to production CDN URL so WP never sideloads relative paths. Never iframe github.io or Add-from-URL github.io assets on wpdev. Assets folder: `public/museum-tour-map/`.

---

## Client Image Specs

| Use case | Recommended size | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Exhibit article featured image | **1920×1080 (16:9)**, saved at 2× retina | Renders max 928×380 via `object-cover` (crops top/bottom on desktop, sides on mobile) — keep subject centered in the middle ~60%. Min 1600×900; floor 1280×720. JPG/WebP, sRGB, under ~500 KB. Photoshop: 1920×1080 px @72ppi, Export As → JPG quality 80. |
| Walk-through 360° panoramas | **6000×3000 (2:1 equirectangular)** | Pannellum pan/zoom needs resolution. Min 4000×2000. WebP under ~3 MB. ⚠️ WordPress auto-scales uploads wider than 2560px (`-scaled` suffix) — host panos outside the media library or disable `big_image_size_threshold` for >2560px. Current originals: Insta360 X3 at 5952×2976 (2:1); two rooms are 2560×1440 off-spec and should be re-exported as 2:1. |

